TRUSTSHIELD AI — Customer Manipulation Pre-Dispatch Defense
Live Working Application: https://trustshield-ai-618809265776.asia-southeast1.run.app/
Synthetic customer manipulation detection and financial protection system preventing social-engineering coercion before payment dispatch.


1. Executive Summary & Problem Statement
Traditional fraud monitoring systems evaluate transactions post-authorization or rely solely on credential theft / unauthorized access indicators (e.g., ATO, stolen card numbers, brute force).
However, modern financial fraud has evolved into Authorized Push Payment (APP) scams and coercive social engineering (e.g., Fake Police/CBI Digital Arrest, Account-Freeze Threats, KYC Extortion, Screen-Share Remote Access). In these attacks:
The customer is authorized and uses their legitimate credentials, device, and biometrics.
The customer is under intense psychological coercion, fear, or urgency.
Money is pushed directly by the customer into mule accounts within seconds, making fund recovery nearly impossible once dispatched.
TRUSTSHIELD AI acts as a pre-dispatch circuit breaker. By evaluating behavioral anomalies, active call/screen-share telemetry, sudden beneficiary addition velocity, and biometric hesitation before funds leave the bank, TRUSTSHIELD intervenes non-custodially, pausing high-risk transactions and neutralizing coercive control.



